---
# OpSy's checks, less those that do not fit test programs:
#
# - readability-magic-numbers, cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers: the
#   literals of a test are its data (sizes, delays, expected values); a name
#   for each would say nothing the line does not.
# - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables: a test shares its
#   state with the tasks and interrupt handlers it starts, which take no
#   arguments.
# - misc-use-internal-linkage: the debugger scenarios and the bench find
#   functions and objects of the tests by name in the ELF.
# - misc-use-anonymous-namespace: OPSY_QEMU_TEST declares a case and its
#   registration, and the case's body follows the macro. A function an
#   anonymous namespace declares cannot be defined outside it, so static is
#   the only internal linkage the macro can give.
# - cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast, performance-no-int-to-ptr,
#   cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic: the QEMU images bring
#   their own startup and probe the hardware. They copy sections between
#   linker symbols, fault at chosen addresses and read the frames the core
#   stacks: addresses are their subject.
# - readability-identifier-length: the objects of a test live a few lines and
#   keep the names its statement gives them (a and b, the two items it
#   orders; f(x), a function and its argument).
# - bugprone-throwing-static-initialization, cert-err58-cpp: the suites
#   register their cases, and OpSy builds its objects, with constructors not
#   marked noexcept; every image builds with -fno-exceptions.
# - IgnoreMacros: the suites' CHECK is a do-while macro, and negates the
#   expression it is given.
# - misc-include-cleaner.MissingIncludes: the tests write durations as
#   std::chrono literals (2ms), as the README does. include-cleaner looks a
#   std symbol up by its identifier, which a literal operator does not have,
#   then falls back to the libstdc++ header that declares it, bits/chrono.h,
#   and asks for that to be included
#   (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/68213). Unused includes are
#   still reported; OpSy's own code keeps the full check.
#
# OpSy's headers are checked under OpSy's configuration (tests/tidy.py
# --headers); a test reports only the headers of the tests.
InheritParentConfig: true
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\\]tests[/\\].*'
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '^$'
Checks: >
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -misc-use-anonymous-namespace,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -cert-err58-cpp
CheckOptions:
  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while.IgnoreMacros: true
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: true
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr.IgnoreMacros: true
  misc-include-cleaner.MissingIncludes: false
...
